  "prediction_postprocess": "adsb-surface-residual-v20-v1",
  "prior_evidence": "Declared after the adsb_v19 screen (docs/adsb_v19_screen/README.md, 18 September): the eleven surface features moved a second-stage LightGBM on the incumbent's residual by -0.002 / -0.148 / -0.146% versus the same model without them (below that screen's 0.3% bar), with the gain on gate and dark rows; a second-stage model itself was worse than the incumbent on every month. This round tests the features where they can act directly: inside the full-data learners (LightGBM group members and combination CatBoosts), whose committee gained -0.06% (v18) and -0.28% (v17) from new members. The user directed on 18 September that minor improvements are worth shipping; the 0.05% + interval rule of adsb_v18_v2 is therefore pre-registered here. Committee base: the nine combination CatBoosts of ens_v18_ctr and the six LightGBMs of ens_v15_lgb (v17's committee), hash-bound. The screen's feature tables were built from matches_v11 (features_v19_screen/); the tables here are built from data/external/adsblol/matches, the learners' own match tables, for all thirteen months. No v20 learner had been fitted before this declaration.",
